Subject: [PATCH 11/15] mb/radxa/x4: Enable S3 resume

The board keeps the LPDDR5 VDD2 rail on from SLP_S4#, while SLP_S3#
turns off the S0 rails, so it supports suspend to RAM. Select
HAVE_ACPI_RESUME: the DSDT then reports _S3, and on resume romstage
runs FSP-M's S3 path with the saved MRC data.

[Generated by Claude, an AI model by Anthropic.]

Signed-off-by: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
---
 src/mainboard/radxa/x4/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/radxa/x4/Kconfig b/src/mainboard/radxa/x4/Kconfig
index 66f1e419..798df07f 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/radxa/x4/Kconfig
+++ b/src/mainboard/radxa/x4/Kconfig
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ config BOARD_SPECIFIC_OPTIONS
 	def_bool y
 	select BOARD_ROMSIZE_KB_16384
 	select FSP_TYPE_IOT
+	select HAVE_ACPI_RESUME
 	select HAVE_ACPI_TABLES
 	select SOC_INTEL_ALDERLAKE_PCH_N
 	select SOC_INTEL_COMMON_BLOCK_HDA_VERB
